({2}^{2}+2(2)+3) \\\\ 29 & =2A+B+11C \\\\ 29 & =2A+(1)+11(2) \\\\ 2A & =29-23 \\\\ A & =\\frac{6}{2} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=3,B=1,$ and $C=2.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+2x+5}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)(x-1)}=\\frac{3x+1}{({x}^{2}+2x+3)}+\\frac{2}{(x-1)}.\n$$" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278737 1017 #edb/ref 17592186278738 13194139534148 true] [17592186278737 1089 "q-102560" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278737 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534148 true] [17592186278737 1100 "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}-5x+12}{(2{x}^{2}+3)(x-3)}=\\frac{x+B}{2{x}^{2}+3}+\\frac{2}{x-3},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $B?$" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278737 1113 #uuid "8ca29016-576b-5531-978a-0e93b6677e56" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278737 1145 "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(2{x}^{2}+3)(x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-5x+12 & =(x+B)(x-3)+2(2{x}^{2}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(0)^{2}-5(0)+12 & =(0+B)(0-3)+2(2(0)^{2}+3) \\\\ 12 & =-3B+6 \\\\ 6 & =-3B \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278739 13194139534148 true] [17592186278738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278740 13194139534148 true] [17592186278738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278741 13194139534148 true] [17592186278738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278742 13194139534148 true] [17592186278738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278743 13194139534148 true] [17592186278738 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534148 true] [17592186278738 1041 "selection" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278738 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278743 13194139534148 true] [17592186278738 1110 #uuid "5a6de8ce-7452-5b79-9a56-e20a20c1d18e" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278739 1034 "-5" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278739 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534148 true] [17592186278739 1111 #uuid "53b23b03-0494-583b-b395-95cf280a3791" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278740 1034 "1" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278740 1103 #