 -59 & =-5B+11(-4) \\\\ 5B & =-44+59 \\\\ B & =\\frac{15}{5} \\\\ B & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to solve for $A,$ we choose $x=1$ and use our results for $B$ and $C.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{2}-22(1)-59 & =(A(1)+B)(1-5)+C({1}^{2}+11) \\\\ 1-22-59 & =-4A-4B+12C \\\\ -80 & =-4A-4(3)+12(-4) \\\\ 4A & =-12-48+80 \\\\ A & =\\frac{20}{4} \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $A=5,$ $B=3,$ and $C=-4.$ Therefore, our final result is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}-22x-59}{({x}^{2}+11)(x-5)}=\\frac{5x+3}{({x}^{2}+11)}-\\frac{4}{(x-5)}.\n$$" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278746 13194139534148 true] [17592186278745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278747 13194139534148 true] [17592186278745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278748 13194139534148 true] [17592186278745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278749 13194139534148 true] [17592186278745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186278750 13194139534148 true] [17592186278745 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534148 true] [17592186278745 1041 "selection" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278745 1104 #edb/ref 17592186278749 13194139534148 true] [17592186278745 1110 #uuid "2da4db48-0dde-5e52-941d-16512a829e1f" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278746 1034 "\\frac{3x+2}{({x}^{2}+11)}+\\frac{2}{(x-5)}" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278746 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534148 true] [17592186278746 1111 #uuid "a3f4ae5f-2a6c-567f-b63c-ad4e4959e404" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278747 1034 "\\frac{2x+5}{({x}^{2}+11)}-\\frac{7}{(x-5)}" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534148 true] [17592186278747 1111 #uuid "ebbb8a3d-56a5-5e10-94a4-7af107198885" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278748 1034 "\\frac{x+2}{({x}^{2}+11)}-\\frac{3}{(x-5)}" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534148 true] [17592186278748 1111 #uuid "e9e61a2e-1e40-5e75-b293-68a9203b6a77" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278749 1034 "\\frac{5x+3}{({x}^{2}+11)}-\\frac{4}{(x-5)}" 13194139534148 true] [17592186278